<task id="024" project="spaarkeai-compose-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-23 enriched compose-selection/compose-document scope descriptions</title>
    <phase>2 LLM Editing Patterns</phase>
    <gate>green</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>phase2-llm</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,api</tags>
    <estimated-effort>high</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Enrich the `compose-selection` and `compose-document` JPS scope `description` fields with behavioral guidance
    (recovery paths, gotchas, examples) per the adeu "tool descriptions ARE the prompt" pattern (design §6.1, §2.0).
    The SAME description text primes the LLM AND renders as the user-visible toolbar/affordance tooltip — author once,
    serve both. This cuts content surface area in half and keeps user/LLM understanding consistent.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    AI prompt/scope author fluent in JPS scope schemas and the "description = prompt = tooltip" discipline.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Updated `compose-selection` and `compose-document` scope definitions whose enriched `description` fields (scope-level
    and per-input-field) carry behavioral guidance that doubles as user-facing tooltip copy, deployed mirror-first to the
    scope catalog location confirmed in Step 2 resource discovery. The BubbleMenu toolbar tooltips (FR-14 / task 030)
    source this same text.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R1 authored these two scopes with rich descriptions (see the R1 notes files below). FR-23 raises them to the
      "tool descriptions = prompt" bar: each description carries recovery paths and gotchas that both prime the model and
      surface as tooltips. This is content authoring, not a new service — no new AI internals, no new dispatch surface.
      Confirm the DEPLOYED scope-catalog location during Step 2 (the R1 files under `notes/jps-scopes/` are drafts; the
      live catalog may be a Dataverse `sprk_analysisscope`-style row and/or a mirror under `infra/dataverse/` — resolve
      before editing so the edit lands on the source of truth, not a stale copy).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file change="modify">compose-selection scope definition (deployed location — CONFIRM in Step 2; draft at projects/spaarkeai-compose-r1/notes/jps-scopes/compose-selection.scope.json)</file>
      <file change="modify">compose-document scope definition (deployed location — CONFIRM in Step 2; draft at projects/spaarkeai-compose-r1/notes/jps-scopes/compose-document.scope.json)</file>
      <file change="reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r1/notes/jps-scopes/compose-selection.scope.json (R1 baseline descriptions to enrich)</file>
      <file change="reference">.claude/catalogs/scope-model-index.json (scope/model catalog index — verify how scopes are catalogued)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="n/a">No task dependency; independent authoring.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">This task authors scope description CONTENT only; it injects no AI internals and adds no dispatch surface (Services/Compose facade discipline unaffected).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">Descriptions describe scope INPUTS/behavior; they do not introduce a parallel routing/config path outside the catalog.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Where the same text renders as a Fluent v9 tooltip (FR-14 toolbar), it must read as concise user help AND as LLM guidance — no hardcoded UI strings elsewhere.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT author new `sprk_analysisplaybook` records — the engine is frozen. This edits SCOPE descriptions only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Mirror-first: if the catalog is Dataverse-backed, edit the `infra/dataverse/inputschemas/` mirror as source of truth per the catalog governance model.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>JPS scope descriptions as prompt + tooltip; scope catalog governance; mirror-first authoring</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/spec.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Tool descriptions ARE the prompt" location="design.md §6.1 / §2.0">Behavioral guidance + recovery paths embedded in scope descriptions; the same text is the LLM prompt AND the user-visible tooltip.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <justification>
    MODIFY existing scope definitions (not a new component) — enriching `description` fields on the two R1 scopes. No new
    surface is introduced. Rule §11 justification is not required for edits to existing surface, but the cost-of-doing-nothing
    is concrete: without enriched descriptions the LLM lacks recovery-path guidance (higher error rate) and the FR-14 toolbar
    tooltips would need separately-authored copy (dual source of truth, drift).
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Context check. Load design §2.0/§6.1 + the R1 baseline scope files.</step>
    <step order="1">Resource discovery: CONFIRM the deployed scope-catalog location (Dataverse row vs `infra/dataverse/` mirror vs BFF-embedded) so edits land on the source of truth. Document the finding in task notes.</step>
    <step order="2">Enrich `compose-selection` scope-level + per-field descriptions with recovery paths, gotchas, and examples that read as both LLM guidance and tooltip copy.</step>
    <step order="3">Enrich `compose-document` scope descriptions likewise, aligned with the FR-22 semantic-appendix enrichment (task 023) so the payload and its description are consistent.</step>
    <step order="4">Ensure each enriched description is concise enough to render as a Fluent v9 tooltip (FR-14) without truncation-of-meaning; note the tooltip-source contract for task 030.</step>
    <step order="5">Validate the scope definitions against their schema (jps-validate or the catalog's validator); confirm no property-level boolean `required` regressions if the catalog shares the OpenAI schema validator.</step>
    <step order="6">Report the deployed-location decision + the "same text primes LLM and renders as tooltip" verification.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="config">compose-selection scope definition (enriched descriptions, at the confirmed deployed location)</output>
    <output type="config">compose-document scope definition (enriched descriptions, at the confirmed deployed location)</output>
    <output type="report">Task completion report incl. deployed-scope-location finding + tooltip-source contract for FR-14</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">`compose-selection` and `compose-document` scope descriptions carry behavioral guidance (recovery paths, gotchas, examples) at scope level and per input field.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The SAME description text is verified to (a) prime the LLM and (b) be consumable as the FR-14 toolbar tooltip — a single authored source, no duplicate copy.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The edit lands on the confirmed deployed catalog source of truth (documented in Step 1), not a stale draft copy.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new `sprk_analysisplaybook` record is created; no new dispatch/config surface is introduced (engine frozen; catalog-governance preserved).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The scope definitions validate against their schema with no property-level boolean `required` violations (NEGATIVE: banned schema shape).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
